3. What's Already Good
• Clean layering with interfaces and constructor injection. OperacionServicio depends only on interfaces (OperacionServicio.cs:20-41 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L20)), the host is the only composition root (ServiceHost.cs:46-97 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/ServiceHost.cs#L46)) and calls _containerDI.Verify() so a missing registration fails at startup rather than at the first tick.
• Parameterized stored-procedure access. Both calls pass values through CrearParametro (OperacionesOUTPK.cs:85-88 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Infraestructura/Repositorio/OperacionesOUTPK.cs#L85), :102-106 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Infraestructura/Repositorio/OperacionesOUTPK.cs#L102)); no SQL is concatenated. No secrets are hard-coded or logged and no cryptography is used.
• Per-item isolation. A failure on one folio is caught inside the loop (OperacionesOUTPK.cs:53-56 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Infraestructura/Repositorio/OperacionesOUTPK.cs#L53)) so one bad operation does not stop the rest of the batch (but see PKDB-FR-6).
• Shutdown is graceful and bounded. TerminacionAsync waits for the startup and running tasks, uses separate wait and cleanup tokens, tolerates a half-initialized host, and disposes the container in a finally (ServiceHost.cs:153-195 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/ServiceHost.cs#L153)).
• Idiomatic tick scope and finalization. Each tick runs in its own AsyncScopedLifestyle scope (ServiceHost.cs:138 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/ServiceHost.cs#L138)) and the service state is released in a finally whose own failure is caught so it cannot mask the primary exception (OperacionServicio.cs:179-190 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L179)).
• Required parameters are parsed through `ParseTimeSpanRequerido` (empty or malformed values throw a named error) and PID handling is safe: Parametrizacion.ObtenerProcesoActualAsync throws if the PID is missing before the .Pid.Value at ServiceHost.cs:120 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/ServiceHost.cs#L120), so GEN-8 is ruled out here.
• A real test project exists (MSTest, fakes, assertions on call counts and on the alert content) and its four cases cover the main orchestration branches: working day, non-working day, out-of-window, and repository failure (SWF_OUT_PK_DB_UT.cs:61-125 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/PruebasUnitarias/SWF_OUT_PK_DB_UT.cs#L61)).
• Repository instances are safe as singletons. RepositorioMaestro creates and disposes a connection per call (using around connection and command), so registering OperacionesOUTPK as a singleton does not share a connection across ticks.
