• File:line: OperacionServicio.cs:125-141 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L125) and :147-156 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L147)
• Current code:
``csharp if (!estaEnHorarioOperacion) // Fuera de Horario { Config.EscribirLog($"INFO|Ejecuta_Procedimientos| El Servicio esta fuera de Horario.", ...); await _IparametrosOperaciones.EnviaAlerta(new AlertaDTO { ..., ClaveAviso = ConstantesClaveAviso.Critico, Descipcion = "Error en ejecuta_procedimientos", Exception = new Exception("El servicio '...' está fuera de horario.") }); return; } ... else { Config.EscribirLog($"ERROR|Ejecuta_Procedimientos| Hoy es un día inhábil.", ...); } ``
• Why it is wrong: being outside the configured window (every night) or on a weekend/holiday is an expected state, not an error. At the 10-second fallback interval that is 360 CRITICAL alert rows per hour outside the window (the shared Alertas.InsertarAlerta does a plain insert with no de-duplication), roughly 8,600 per night, plus a CRITICAL row whose description says "Error en ejecuta_procedimientos" for a non-error. Identical rows bury genuine alerts (such as the one in FR-1 if it were ever raised) and can become a notification storm if a notifier consumes the table. The non-business-day branch logs an ERROR per tick without an alert. The test suite asserts this behavior (SWF_OUT_PK_DB_UT.cs:101 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/PruebasUnitarias/SWF_OUT_PK_DB_UT.cs#L101)), so the defect is locked in.
• Recommended code: treat the window as a Skipped state: log INFO only on the transition (the service already tracks BHorarioLectura for exactly this, lines 108-122), raise at most one alert per transition or per day, and log the non-business-day skip at INFO:
``csharp if (!estaEnHorarioOperacion) { return; // transition already logged above; no alert for an expected state } if (_configuracion.EsDiaHabil != true) { Config.EscribirLog("INFO|Ejecuta_Procedimientos|Dia inhabil: sin procesamiento.", ...); return; } await _iOperacionesOUTPK.InsertaMensajesPKDB(); `` Update the test to assert "no alert while out of window".
• Benefit: a quiet alert table and logs, and alerts that mean something.
• Suggested JIRA: PKDB-4 (High)
PKDB-FR-5 (Medium) - The first four database calls of a tick run outside the try/catch/finally, so their failures skip the alert and the finalization (GEN-7)
• File:line: OperacionServicio.cs:51-65 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/Aplicacion/OperacionServicio.cs#L51) (the try starts at line 67)
