• Why it is wrong: the service state is set to "running" first. If parametrosSistema(), ObtenerFechaSistemaAsync() or BEsDiaHabil() throws (for example, a database timeout, the most likely transient failure), the exception skips the catch (no alert, no Exito handling) and the finally (the state stays "en ejecución" until the next successful tick). Only the host's last-resort catch logs it (ServiceHost.cs:144-147 (../../SWIFT/Outgoing/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/SWF_OUT_PK_DB/ServiceHost.cs#L144)). The same method's catch also awaits EnviaAlerta unguarded, so when the database is down the alert insert fails too and replaces the original exception.
